  "explanation": "The documents explicitly state that Anna Palaiologina (daughter of Andronikos Angelos Palaiologos) was married to John II Orsini (D1S1, D1S4-D1S6, D3S2-D3S4) and later married John Komnenos Asen (D1S2, D4S11). Other names in the input (Manuel II Palaiologos, Thomas Preljubović, John VIII Palaiologos, Andronikos III Palaiologos) are associated with different individuals named Anna (e.g., Anna of Moscow, Anna of Savoy) or represent conflicting/modified claims in specific documents (like D5 which notes a modification to the context) that contradict the primary biographical accounts found in D1 and D3. Specifically, D4S9 contains a factual error claiming she was the wife of Manuel II Palaiologos, which is contradicted by the consistent evidence of her marriage to John II Orsini and John Komnenos Asen. D5S3 explicitly states the context was modified to suggest a marriage to Thomas Preljubović, indicating this is a hypothetical or altered scenario rather than the established fact supported by the majority of the text. Therefore, only the two historically attested spouses are returned."
